Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:35:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] completion : keep a failed report file instead of
 removing it by name

After the exclusive create, another process can rename the file and put
an unrelated file at the same path; removing by name could delete it. A
failed write now leaves the empty or partial file and returns nonzero,
consumers reject it (documented rule, also checks the exit status).

Require std::atomic<int> to be always lock-free where the signal handler
is built.

Tests: fdopen hook in the shim that moves the new report and puts an
unrelated file at its path, before fdopen or write failure; a new run
dir per test invocation so earlier case dirs are never removed.

Request: public-completion-report-20261016-01

